cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "spheropack: random sphere packings with the event-driven Lubachevsky-Stillinger algorithm"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-01"
message: "If you use spheropack in your work, please cite the version you used."
authors:
  - family-names: Peters
    given-names: E.A.J.F.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6099-3583"
abstract: >-
  spheropack generates random sphere packings in periodic boxes, slabs, cylinders and
  spherical containers with an exact event-driven Lubachevsky-Stillinger algorithm
  (header-only C++20 core, Python interface), including a quasi-static jamming protocol
  and structure analysis. It also provides the rejection-free event-driven Monte Carlo
  method of Peters and de With (2012).
keywords:
  - sphere packing
  - random close packing
  - jamming
  - event-driven molecular dynamics
  - Lubachevsky-Stillinger
  - packed beds
  - chemical engineering
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/computational-chemical-engineering/spheropack"
url: "https://computational-chemical-engineering.github.io/spheropack"
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Peters
        given-names: E.A.J.F.
      - family-names: de With
        given-names: G.
    title: "Rejection-free Monte Carlo sampling for general potentials"
    journal: "Physical Review E"
    volume: 85
    start: "026703"
    year: 2012
    doi: 10.1103/PhysRevE.85.026703
